== (4) necklace splitting of the doubled -17 cycle word ==
 word (1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4): 14 beads, 3 types; a split with cuts at (1, 2, 7) and pieces assigned (0, 0, 0, 1) gives thief A the pieces [(1,), (1,), (1, 2, 1, 1, 4)]
 both thieves get {1: 5, 2: 1, 4: 1}; the shares are unions of intervals, not orbit segments, so they carry no dynamics (Alon's bound k(q-1) = 3 cuts attained here with 3)
